KB-277 D21 kind/adapter namespace probe (which allow band form wins the
grant, match versus no-match shapes observed in run events).

This step's allow_tools bands are exactly ["bash:printf *",
"adapter.copilot.main.tools.*"]: a kind-prefixed argument band over the
command segment of a bash-kind tool call, and an adapter-namespace trailing
band. The FIRST matching band wins and the grant echoes the winning pattern.

Make precisely this three-call sequence:

(1) Call the bash tool now, precisely once:

        command: printf d21d-kind-prefixed-band > ./d21d_record

    A command tool call of bash kind. On this adapter the policy tool name
    for the command tool is `shell`, so the bash-prefixed band and the
    adapter-namespace band are both expected to match nothing.

(2) Call the view tool now, precisely once, on the file ../harness_contracts_v1/main.chcl

    The read-kind call matches neither band; expect the permission denied
    result, then continue.

(3) Call the submit_outcome tool now, precisely once — the approved outcome
    declares a reason payload schema, so use the payload lane:

        outcome = "approved"
        payload = {"reason": "D21 kind-prefixed bands: the grant echoes which band won (kind-prefixed argument form versus adapter namespace form), the unmatched call was denied, and the step finalized approved after recovering"}
        comment = "D21 kind-prefix probe"

No other tools, no other calls.